---
import LessonPage from "../../../components/lesson/LessonPage.astro";
import { defineLesson } from "../../../data/lesson-schema.mjs";
export const page = defineLesson({
  "title": "Animals · A0 Vocabulary · Curriculum Map",
  "slug": "animals",
  "level": "A0",
  "topic": "Animals",
  "category": "Vocabulary & Topics",
  "contentType": "vocabulary",
  "status": "ready",
  "description": "Name common animals with a or an : a dog , an elephant . Then talk about one or many: The cat is small. The dogs are big. Finish with real life: I have a cat. My neighbor has two d",
  "sequence": 15,
  "prerequisites": [],
  "related": [],
  "assessments": [
    "a0-exit"
  ]
});
---
<LessonPage page={page}>
<main class="wrap">
  <p class="kicker"><span class="dot"></span> Vocabulary · Lesson 16</p>
  <h1>Animals</h1>
  <p class="standfirst">Name common animals with <span class="ex">a</span> or <span class="ex">an</span>: <span class="ex">a dog</span>, <span class="ex">an elephant</span>. Then talk about one or many: <span class="ex">The cat is small. The dogs are big.</span> Finish with real life: <span class="ex">I have a cat. My neighbor has two dogs.</span></p>
  <div class="meta-row">
    <span class="tag">≈ 45–55 min</span>
    <span class="tag">a / an</span>
    <span class="tag">one / many</span>
    <span class="tag">10 interactive tasks</span>
  </div>

  <div class="lesson-flow" aria-label="Lesson flow">
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Notice</b><span>One animal or two? Listen to is and are.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Discover</b><span>a or an, and the plural -s with are.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Build</b><span>Match, choose, read, and build chunks.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Use</b><span>Talk about the animals in your life.</span></div>
  </div>

  <p class="note-line">Most animal words add <span class="ex">-s</span> for “many”: <span class="ex">dog → dogs, cat → cats, bird → birds</span>. After a number, the noun is plural: <span class="ex">two dogs, three cats</span>.</p>

  <h2>Meet the animals</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>Point to each picture and say the word with <span class="ex">a</span> or <span class="ex">an</span>.</p>
  <div class="figure-grid">
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/cat.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">a cat</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/dog.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">a dog</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/bird.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">a bird</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/fish.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">a fish</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/rabbit.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">a rabbit</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/pig.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">a pig</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/cow.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">a cow</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/elephant.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">an elephant</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/horse.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">a horse</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/sheep.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">a sheep</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/duck.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">a duck</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/monkey.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">a monkey</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/lion.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">a lion</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/tiger.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">a tiger</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/bear.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">a bear</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/owl.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">an owl</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/frog.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">a frog</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/snake.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">a snake</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/turtle.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">a turtle</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/penguin.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">a penguin</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/chicken.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">a chicken</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/fox.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">a fox</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/panda.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">a panda</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/giraffe.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">a giraffe</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/zebra.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">a zebra</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/octopus.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">an octopus</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/dolphin.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">a dolphin</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/koala.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">a koala</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/kangaroo.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">a kangaroo</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/crocodile.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">a crocodile</span></div>
  </div>

  <h2>Notice before the rule</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>One animal or two?</h3>
    <p><span class="ex">I have a dog. My dog is big.</span><br /><span class="ex">My neighbor has two cats. The cats are small.</span></p>
    <ul>
      <li>Look at <strong>dog</strong> and <strong>cats</strong>. What is at the end of <strong>cats</strong>?</li>
      <li>After <strong>my dog</strong> we say <span class="ex">is</span>. After <strong>the cats</strong> we say a different word. Which word?</li>
      <li>Say these aloud: <span class="ex">a cat, a dog, an elephant, an owl</span>. When do we say <span class="ex">an</span> instead of <span class="ex">a</span>?</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill>
    <h3>Discovery check: one or many?</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">Say the sentence aloud first. One animal takes a / an and is. Many animals take -s and are.</p>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Answer choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="a">a</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="an">an</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="is">is</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="are">are</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>I have <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="a" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> dog. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(first sound: d)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>At the zoo I see <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="an" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> elephant. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(first sound: e)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>The cat <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="is" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> black. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(one cat)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>The dogs <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="are" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> friendly. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(two dogs)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>In the tree there is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="an" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> owl. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(first sound: o)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>They <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="are" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> horses. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(many horses)</span></span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>The system: name the animal, count the animal</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>Each animal word is a <strong>noun</strong>. Two small rules work for all of them:</p>
  <p><strong>1. One animal?</strong> &nbsp;Use <span class="ex">a</span> before a consonant sound, <span class="ex">an</span> before a vowel sound, and say <span class="ex">is</span>: <span class="ex">a dog · an elephant · The dog is big.</span></p>
  <p><strong>2. More than one?</strong> &nbsp;Drop <span class="ex">a / an</span>, add <span class="ex">-s</span>, and say <span class="ex">are</span>: <span class="ex">two dogs · The dogs are big.</span></p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>one (singular)</th><th>many (plural)</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><b>a</b> dog &nbsp;·&nbsp; the dog <b>is</b> big</td><td>two <b>dogs</b> &nbsp;·&nbsp; the dogs <b>are</b> big</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>a</b> cat &nbsp;·&nbsp; the cat <b>is</b> small</td><td>three <b>cats</b> &nbsp;·&nbsp; the cats <b>are</b> small</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>an</b> owl &nbsp;·&nbsp; it <b>is</b> an owl</td><td>two <b>owls</b> &nbsp;·&nbsp; they <b>are</b> owls</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <div class="note">
    <h3>Meaning check</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Can we say <span class="ex">the dogs is big</span>? <strong>No.</strong> Two dogs are many, so we say <span class="ex">the dogs are big</span>.</li>
      <li>Can we say <span class="ex">two cat</span>? <strong>No.</strong> After a number we need the plural: <span class="ex">two cats</span>.</li>
      <li>Two special words do not change: <span class="ex">one sheep, two sheep</span> and <span class="ex">one fish, two fish</span>.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <h2>Animal words in real chunks</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>People talk about animals in short chunks. Keep these together:</p>
  <p><span class="ex">I have a dog. &nbsp; · &nbsp; I don’t have a pet. &nbsp; · &nbsp; I like cats.</span><br /><span class="ex">It’s a cat. &nbsp; · &nbsp; It is small and black. &nbsp; · &nbsp; They are friendly.</span></p>
  <p>And chunks about other people: <span class="ex">My neighbor has two dogs. &nbsp; · &nbsp; My friend has a bird.</span></p>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill>
    <h3>Drill 1: choose the animal from the clue</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">Read the clue, then choose the animal that fits</p>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Answer choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="dog">dog</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="cat">cat</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="horse">horse</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="fish">fish</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="sheep">sheep</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="lion">lion</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="bird">bird</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="chicken">chicken</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>People ride it. → a <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="horse" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>It gives us wool. → a <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="sheep" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>It lives in water and can swim. → a <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="fish" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>It is a very big cat. People call it the king of animals. → a <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="lion" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>Many people walk it in the park every day. → a <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="dog" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>It is a small pet. It says “meow.” → a <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="cat" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">7</span><span>It is small and can fly from tree to tree. → a <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="bird" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">8</span><span>It is a farm bird. It gives us eggs. → a <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="chicken" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button></span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Build the meaning, then the sentence</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>

  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-game>
    <h3>Drill 2: match each animal to a true description</h3>
    <p class="tile-target">Tap an animal, then tap the description that fits it</p>
    <div class="tile-bank">
      <button class="tile" data-tile="elephant">an elephant</button>
      <button class="tile" data-tile="fish">a fish</button>
      <button class="tile" data-tile="bird">a bird</button>
      <button class="tile" data-tile="rabbit">a rabbit</button>
      <button class="tile" data-tile="cow">a cow</button>
      <button class="tile" data-tile="giraffe">a giraffe</button>
      <button class="tile" data-tile="penguin">a penguin</button>
    </div>
    <div class="slot-board">
      <button class="slot" data-slot="elephant" data-placeholder="it is big, with a long trunk">it is big, with a long trunk</button>
      <button class="slot" data-slot="fish" data-placeholder="it lives in water">it lives in water</button>
      <button class="slot" data-slot="bird" data-placeholder="it is small, and it can fly">it is small, and it can fly</button>
      <button class="slot" data-slot="rabbit" data-placeholder="it has long ears">it has long ears</button>
      <button class="slot" data-slot="cow" data-placeholder="it gives us milk">it gives us milk</button>
      <button class="slot" data-slot="giraffe" data-placeholder="it has a very long neck">it has a very long neck</button>
      <button class="slot" data-slot="penguin" data-placeholder="it is black and white, and it cannot fly">it is black and white, and it cannot fly</button>
    </div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-tiles>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-tiles>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="the dogs are very friendly">
    <h3>Drill 3: talk about two dogs</h3>
    <p class="tile-target">Your neighbor’s dogs are friendly. Build the sentence, then say it.</p>
    <div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="friendly">friendly</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="the">The</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="are">are</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="very">very</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="dogs">dogs</button>
    </div>
    <div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap words in order"></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="she has a small cat">
    <h3>Drill 4: talk about a friend’s pet</h3>
    <p class="tile-target">Your friend has one small cat. Build the sentence, then say it.</p>
    <div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="cat">cat</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="she">She</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="small">small</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="has">has</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="a">a</button>
    </div>
    <div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap words in order"></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Read and choose</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>A message about the neighbor’s pets</h3>
    <p><span class="ex">“My neighbor has two dogs and a cat. The dogs are big and very friendly. The cat is small and black. Her name is Luna.”</span></p>
  </div>
  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Good reading. You understood a real message about animals.">
    <h3>Drill 5: read, then choose</h3>
    <div class="quiz-list">
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="two">
        <p class="quiz-question">1. How many dogs does the neighbor have?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="one">one</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="two">two</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="three">three</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="big and friendly">
        <p class="quiz-question">2. The dogs are ___.</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="big and friendly">big and friendly</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="small and black">small and black</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="old and slow">old and slow</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="the cat">
        <p class="quiz-question">3. Who is Luna?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the cat">the cat</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="a dog">a dog</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the neighbor">the neighbor</button></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-quiz>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-quiz>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Notice and repair errors</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="are" data-fix="The cat is black." data-why="One cat is singular, so we use is, not are.">
    <h3>Drill 6: one cat, is or are?</h3>
    <p>Tap the word that is wrong.</p>
    <div class="spot-options">
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="the">The</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="cat">cat</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="are">are</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="black">black.</button>
    </div>
    <p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="dog" data-fix="I have two dogs." data-why="After a number we use the plural, so dog becomes dogs.">
    <h3>Drill 7: one or many?</h3>
    <p>Tap the word that does not match the number.</p>
    <div class="spot-options">
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="i">I</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="have">have</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="two">two</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="dog">dog.</button>
    </div>
    <p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="micro-drill" data-transform>
    <h3>Drill 8: one animal, many animals</h3>
    <p>Say the new sentence aloud first. Reveal only after you answer.</p>
    <div class="transform-list">
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>1</b> The dog is big. &nbsp;→&nbsp; make it two dogs</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>The dogs are big.</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>2</b> The cat is small. &nbsp;→&nbsp; make it three cats</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>The cats are small.</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>3</b> It is a bird. &nbsp;→&nbsp; make it many</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>They are birds.</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>4</b> The horse is fast. &nbsp;→&nbsp; make it two horses</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>The horses are fast.</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>5</b> They are rabbits. &nbsp;→&nbsp; make it one</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>It is a rabbit.</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>6</b> I have a dog. &nbsp;→&nbsp; make it two</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>I have two dogs.</strong></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Use it in real life</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Talk about you:</b> Do you have a pet? Say <span class="ex">I have a cat. She is small and gray.</span> If not: <span class="ex">I don’t have a pet, but I like dogs.</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Your street:</b> Name three animals you see near your home or in your city, with <span class="ex">a</span> or <span class="ex">an</span>: <span class="ex">a bird, a dog, a cat.</span> Then count one of them: <span class="ex">I see two dogs every morning.</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>A friend’s pet:</b> Talk about a pet in your family or a friend’s pet. <span class="ex">My friend has a dog. It is big and brown. It is very friendly.</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>At the zoo or on a farm:</b> You visit the city zoo or a farm outside town. Say three animals you want to see: <span class="ex">I want to see the lions, the elephants, and the penguins.</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Information gap:</b> Describe an animal in two short sentences and the teacher guesses. Then change roles. <span class="ex">It is big. It lives in water.</span></div>

  <h2>Reflect</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Explain the choice</h3>
    <p>Complete this aloud: “For one animal I say <strong>a</strong> or <strong>an</strong> and use <strong>is</strong>: <span class="ex">the cat ___ small</span>. For many animals I add ______ and use ______: <span class="ex">the dogs ___ big</span>.”</p>
    <p>Then say one true sentence about an animal in your life: a pet, a neighbor’s pet, or an animal on your street.</p>
  </div>

